    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "6d75fd6f-2fae-3ed6-ab55-43b62f17dbc6",
                "word": "holotype",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "92524d8f-a296-4af9-8b07-54ab1104d617",
                        "entry_id": "6d75fd6f-2fae-3ed6-ab55-43b62f17dbc6",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "holotypes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2ee0f17a-9aaa-38da-9bb5-9d546b017f05",
                        "entry_id": "6d75fd6f-2fae-3ed6-ab55-43b62f17dbc6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The single physical example (or illustration) of an organism used to formally describe the species (or lower-order taxon), subsequently to be kept as a reference."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4f7ae328-016a-4a80-8c3e-3d534d843a20",
                                "sense_id": "2ee0f17a-9aaa-38da-9bb5-9d546b017f05",
                                "text": "The holotype of this species is subglobular in shape and ammoniticonic in its mode of growth."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a34c5c2b-3aea-4df8-bcd3-63f494a029b9",
                                "sense_id": "2ee0f17a-9aaa-38da-9bb5-9d546b017f05",
                                "text": "The surface of the holotype bears seven rounded annulations which slope very slightly orad from the venter."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c5a4dc4f-6116-4f8a-96ab-371a8480dee6",
                                "sense_id": "2ee0f17a-9aaa-38da-9bb5-9d546b017f05",
                                "text": "Primary types include holotypes, lectotypes, and neotypes, while all other types (e.g., paratypes) are secondary types. A holotype is a unique, name-bearing type specimen designated by the original author. The holotype is the single individual of a species that serves as a voucher for a given species name. A holotype can be designated only by the original author and in the publication in which that author established its name."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "654544a0-2211-4eab-9d1c-16013bb23006",
                                "sense_id": "2ee0f17a-9aaa-38da-9bb5-9d546b017f05",
                                "text": "The species to which the holotype belongs is then referred to by the name proposed by the author, at least when the same name has not previously been applied to another species.[…]If his specimen is not the same species as any of the holotypes preserved in museums, he should prepare a description of his specimen and have it published with his proposed name for the new species or give it to a specialist who is interested in doing this."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a0088b93-0305-4f01-963e-3fe02f0e3a51",
                        "source_entry_id": "6d75fd6f-2fae-3ed6-ab55-43b62f17dbc6",
                        "source_sense_id": "2ee0f17a-9aaa-38da-9bb5-9d546b017f05",
                        "source_sense_description": "single physical example or illustration of an organism used to describe the taxon",
                        "target_lang_word": "holotype",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "holotype",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2536e330-6797-36d4-80b4-19fb9da676a5",
                                        "entry_id": "90773fd3-00ad-3dd7-a6fc-891c26899a46",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Spécimen de référence (conservé) qui a servi à la description d’une nouvelle espèce."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6026097a-f53c-4d3c-a647-c991cd57ed06",
                                                "sense_id": "2536e330-6797-36d4-80b4-19fb9da676a5",
                                                "text": "De même, Wernli suggère une paroi calcaire hyaline radiée partiellement recristallisée, peut-être perforée sur la base des illustrations de l’holotype."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca4069ec-9382-4f3a-bf6f-088fa4369a42",
                                                "sense_id": "2536e330-6797-36d4-80b4-19fb9da676a5",
                                                "text": "C’est ainsi que, par exemple, les pièces paléoanthropologiques extrêmement importantes, holotypes de ce qu’il [Camille Arambourg] a appelé l’Atlanthropus mauritanicus, Homo erectus maghrébin de 700 000 ans, extraites de ses fouilles à Ternifine (Tighennif) en Algérie en 1953-1954, font partie des collections du Muséum de Paris."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7ac3f66-b2dd-46b5-ba51-890f24843e4e",
                                                "sense_id": "2536e330-6797-36d4-80b4-19fb9da676a5",
                                                "text": "Le muséum possède un nombre hallucinant d’holotypes dans son herbier."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
